- entry .Nominative   the typeclass which gives a plane its rules: `plane is Nominative under rules`
+ entry .Nominative   la clase de tipos que da sus reglas a un plano: `plane is Nominative under rules`

= entry .Nominative   the typeclass which gives a plane its rules: `plane is Nominative under rules`
-   detail
+   detail

-       A `Nominative` is a `Typeclass` whose `Self` is the plane and whose `Limit` (from
-       `Limited`, written with the `under` alias) is the plane's rules: an intersection of
-       `Check` types, each a rule applied to a literal, such as
-       `MustNotContain["/"] & MustNotEqual["."] & MustNotEqual[".."] & MustNotEqual[""]`. The
-       macros behind `n"…"`, `Name[plane](text)` and `text.as[Name[plane]]` summon the given
-       for a plane and read its `Limit` type to find which rules to run, in the order they
-       are written.
+       Un `Nominative` es un `Typeclass` cuyo `Self` es el plano y cuyo `Limit` (de `Limited`,
+       escrito con el alias `under`) son las reglas del plano: una intersección de tipos
+       `Check`, cada uno una regla aplicada a un literal, como
+       `MustNotContain["/"] & MustNotEqual["."] & MustNotEqual[".."] & MustNotEqual[""]`. Las
+       macros que hay detrás de `n"…"`, `Name[plane](text)` y `text.as[Name[plane]]` convocan el
+       given de un plano y leen su tipo `Limit` para saber qué reglas ejecutar, en el orden en
+       que están escritas.

